SUMMARY:Colin Stetson & Brìghde Chaimbeul
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:Colin Stetson and Brìghde Chaimbeul come together on All the L
 ight in the World\, a collaborative album that feels both ancient and imme
 diate. Built from deep listening\, improvisation\, and an instinct for emo
 tional intensity\, the record merges Stetson’s innovative approach to th
 e saxophone with Chaimbeul’s singular command of the Scottish smallpipes
 \, creating music that drifts between drone\, ritual\, and cinematic expan
 se.\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/colin-stetson-brighde-chaimbeul/\nFr
 om Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/colin-stetson-brighde-chaimbeul/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3a404d21c876a246e718d7a666d9b50c8752ff32@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20260915T220442Z
DTSTART:20260924T230000Z
DTEND:20260925T010000Z
SUMMARY:The Artist’s Voice: Njideka Akunyili Crosby with Ruth Erickson
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:Internationally acclaimed artist Njideka Akunyili Crosby has be
 en selected to create the first official portrait of President Barack Obam
 a and First Lady Michelle Obama for the Obama Presidential Center opening 
 in Chicago in summer 2026. Audiences familiar with Crosby’s captivating 
 works\, including “The Beautyful Ones” Series #7 on view in the ICA’
 s galleries\, recognize the artist’s exquisite and densely layered surfa
 ces that incorporate painting\, drawing\, collage\, photo\, and printmakin
 g to reflect on the importance of the dailyness of life. Join ICA’s Barb
 ara Lee Chief Curator Ruth Erickson for an engaging conversation with Cros
 by\, as the artist reflects on her creative process\, her ongoing explorat
 ion of hope and optimism in The Beautyful Ones series\, and the significan
 ce of her latest historic commission.\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/th
 e-artists-voice-njideka-akunyili-crosby-with-ruth-erickson/\nFrom Pushpin 
 Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/the-artists-voice-njideka-akunyili-cro
 sby-with-ruth-erickson/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1bd19a5cc73082fac3586a885dd4b057eb8aa34b@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20260915T220442Z
DTSTART:20260926T000000Z
DTEND:20260926T020000Z
SUMMARY:anaiis with special guest ToriTori
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:London-based polymath anaiis makes the kind of music that speak
 s to an innate sense of wonder. On her most recent album Devotion & The Bl
 ack Divine\, the songs swell with emotional clarity as she lovingly pushes
  herself beyond the edges of her comfort zone. anaiis seems to be in conve
 rsation with the reverence of nature\, recognizing our own divinity\, and 
 therefore our wholeness in both chaos and beauty. New motherhood deepened 
 anaiis’ understanding of how to react with grace\, create with freedom\,
  and captures the reality of being human\, unposed and unpredictable. That
  internal expansion is audible across the record. It leans into the idea t
 hat selfhood is something in motion\; much like Octavia Butler’s reminde
 r that “God is Change. Everything you touch you change\, everything you 
 change\, changes you.”\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/anaiis/\nFrom P
 ushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/anaiis/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6ba5ba261e0784787137c818e384f59b51b6d559@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20260915T220442Z
DTSTART:20260927T140000Z
DTEND:20260927T160000Z
SUMMARY:The Artist’s Voice: Lucy Raven with Ruth Erickson
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:Raven’s work explores the physical and mythical landscapes of
  the American West\, as seen in her mesmerizing film installation—Murder
 ers Bar. Witness the transformation of a landscape and embrace the subsequ
 ent release of energy and force through the largest dam removal project in
  North America. Join Raven and Ruth Erickson\, Barbara Lee Chief Curator a
 nd Director of Curatorial Affairs at the ICA\, in East Boston’s Watershe
 d for a morning conversation about her ongoing work centering industry and
  the American landscape. Coffee and breakfast snacks will be provided\, as
  supplies last.\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/the-artists-voice-lucy-r
 aven-with-ruth-erickson/\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston
 /
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/the-artists-voice-lucy-raven-with-ruth
 -erickson/
END:VEVENT
