SUMMARY:TCB – The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizing
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:The ICA\, in partnership with the Boston Ujima Project\, presen
 ts a special screening of TCB – The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizi
 ng\, a biography of the influential writer\, filmmaker and cultural worker
 \, who with humor and deep insight\, inspired a generation of artists to d
 edicate themselves to community empowerment. The film is structured as a s
 eries of lessons on cultural organizing\, gleaned from Bambara’s life an
 d shared by her friends\, colleagues and students.\nhttps://www.icaboston.
 org/events/tcb-the-toni-cade-bambara-school-of-organizing/\nFrom Pushpin B
 oston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/tcb-the-toni-cade-bambara-school-of-or
 ganizing/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1b2e391d14ae09d77fc8ebfc3799b6c4262a4e8d@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20260915T220442Z
DTSTART:20261015T230000Z
DTEND:20261016T010000Z
SUMMARY:The Artist’s Voice: Tony Oursler with Susan Goldberg\, Meghan Cla
 re Considine\, and Nora Burnett Abrams
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:What does access to art look like? Today\, anyone with an inter
 net connection can explore art from around the world in seconds. But long 
 before streaming and social media transformed how we can experience cultur
 e\, a collaboration in Boston was already imagining a new way to bring con
 temporary art into people’s homes.\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/the
 -artists-voice-tony-oursler-with-susan-goldberg-meghan-clare-considine-and
 -nora-burnett-abrams/\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/the-artists-voice-tony-oursler-with-su
 san-goldberg-meghan-clare-considine-and-nora-burnett-abrams/
END:VEVENT
